<!--
    Per-function extrapop: `option extrapop <n> <name>`.

    OptionExtraPop (decompiler/cpp/options.cc) with a function name sets that
    function's prototype extrapop, which every caller copies into its call
    spec (ActionDefaultParams). kuna returned "Unknown function name" for
    every name.

    Authored x86-32 (nasm): f pushes 2 and 1, calls g, then returns [esp+4];
    g ends in `ret 8`. The gcc cspec's extrapop (4) leaves the arguments on
    the stack, so [esp+4] reads the pushed 2. With extrapop 12 for g the
    stack pointer is back at f's entry and [esp+4] is f's own argument.

    Pass 1 (model extrapop): `g(1); return 2;`
    Pass 2 (`option extrapop 12 g`): `g(1,2); return a0;`

-->
